13:T592,Inflation rose last month as the price of gas, groceries and airfares jumped while new data showed applications for unemployment aid soared, putting the Federal Reserve in an increasingly tough spot as it prepares to cut rates at its meeting next week despite persistent price pressures.  Consumer prices increased 2. 9% in August from a year earlier, the Labor Department said Thursday, up from 2. 7% the previous month and the biggest jump since January.  Excluding the volatile food and energy categories, core prices rose 3. 1%, the same as in July.  Both figures are above the Federal Reserve’s 2% target.  A separate government report Thursday showed that weekly applications for unemployment aid jumped 27,000 to 263,000, the highest in nearly four years.  Requests for jobless benefits are a proxy for layoffs.  Recent reports have also showed that hiring has weakened dramatically this year and was lower than previously estimated last year.  The data raises the specter of “stagflation,” a trend that last bedeviled the U. S.  economy in the 1970s.  The term refers to a period of slower growth, higher unemployment along with rising inflation.  It is unusual because a weak economy typically keeps inflation in check.  Such a scenario could create major headaches for the Fed as it prepares for a meeting next week, when policymakers are widely expected to cut their short-term rate to about 4. 1% from 4. 3%.4:[["$","$Lf",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"NewsArticle\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/business/inflation-jobless-claims-fed-challenge/\"},\"headline\":\"Inflation and a weak job market strain the Fed and Americans.\",\"description\":\"Inflation rose in August while jobless claims surged, creating a tricky situation for the Fed as it plans interest-rate cuts amid persistent price pressures and tariff-driven cost increases.\",\"image\":\"/images/inflation-fed-tariffs.webp\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Lauren Jacobs\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/our-team/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"PressoraHub\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://www.pressorahub.com/images/pressorahub-icon.webp\"}},\"datePublished\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2025-06-18T00:00:00.000Z\"}"}}],["$","$L10",null,{"breadcrumbTitle":"Inflation and a weak job market strain the Fed and Americans.","category":"business","children":["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"post-layout-1 padding","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"top-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"post-card single-card","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-content","children":[["$","$L11",null,{"title":"inflation-jobless-claims-fed-challenge","href":"/business","className":"card-btn bg-green","children":"business"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"title","style":{"lineHeight":1.3},"children":"Inflation and a weak job market strain the Fed and Americans."}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"post-list","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"author","children":["by ",["$","span",null,{"children":"Lauren Jacobs"}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"date","children":"September 12, 2025"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Inflation rose in August while jobless claims surged, creating a tricky situation for the Fed as it plans interest-rate cuts amid persistent price pressures and tariff-driven cost increases."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"post-social","children":["$","ul",null,{"className":"social-list d-flex align-items-center","children":[["$","li",null,{}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://www.instagram.com/laur.enjacobs001/","className":"instagram","title":"instagram","children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-instagram"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://medium.com/@lauren_jacobs","className":"","style":{"border":""},"children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-medium"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://substack.com/@laurenjacobs672308","className":"pinterest","children":["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"20","height":"15","viewBox":"0 0 256 256","children":["$","g",null,{"transform":"scale(5.12,5.12)","children":[["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,11h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,19h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,44.805l-17.016,-10.636l-17.984,10.579v-23.748h35z"}]]}]}]}]}]]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"col-lg-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-layout-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"layout-thumb mb-30","children":["$","$L12",null,{"title":"Inflation and a weak job market strain the Fed and Americans.","src":"/images/inflation-fed-tariffs.webp","alt":"Inflation and a weak job market strain the Fed and Americans.","width":1200,"height":800,"priority":true,"style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto"}}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"layout-desc","style":{"marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"$13"}],"$L14","$L15","$L16"]}],"$L17","$L18"]}]}],"$L19"]}]]}]}],"$L1a"]}]}]]
